1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:13,380
What two interruptions did the writer have?
作者受到了哪两次打扰？

2
00:00:13,380 --> 00:00:17,530
What two interruptions did the writer have?
作者受到了哪两次打扰？

3
00:00:20,070 --> 00:00:25,730
After breakfast, I sent the children to school and then I went to the shops.
早饭后，我送孩子们上学，然后去买东西。

4
00:00:27,290 --> 00:00:30,140
It was still early when I returned home.
我回到家时天还早。

5
00:00:31,460 --> 00:00:36,770
The children were at school, my husband was at work and the house was quiet.
孩子们在上学，丈夫在上班，家里很安静。

6
00:00:37,950 --> 00:00:41,220
So I decided to make some meat pies.
于是我决定做几个肉馅饼。

7
00:00:42,670 --> 00:00:46,300
In a short time I was busy mixing butter
不一会儿我就忙着把黄油

8
00:00:46,320 --> 00:00:51,200
and flour and my hands were soon covered with sticky pastry.
和面粉搅在一起，手上很快就沾满了黏糊糊的面团。

9
00:00:52,560 --> 00:00:56,330
At exactly that moment, the telephone rang.
就在这时，电话铃响了。

10
00:00:57,070 --> 00:00:59,520
Nothing could have been more annoying.
没有比这更恼人的了。

11
00:01:00,590 --> 00:01:07,530
I picked up the receiver between two sticky fingers and was dismayed when
我用两根黏糊糊的手指拿起听筒，

12
00:01:07,550 --> 00:01:10,150
I recognized the voice of Helen Bates.
听出海伦·贝茨的声音时，感到很沮丧。

13
00:01:10,970 --> 00:01:18,320
It took me ten minutes to persuade her to ring back later. At last I hung up the receiver.
我花了十分钟才说服她过会儿再打来。最后我挂上了听筒。

14
00:01:18,770 --> 00:01:24,200
What a mess! There was pastry on my fingers,
真是一团糟！我的手指上、

15
00:01:24,330 --> 00:01:26,580
on the telephone, and on the doorknobs.
电话上和门把手上都是面团。

16
00:01:27,870 --> 00:01:34,800
I had no sooner got back to the kitchen than the doorbell rang loud enough to wake the dead.
我刚回到厨房，门铃就响了起来，响得足以把死人吵醒。

17
00:01:35,340 --> 00:01:41,370
This time it was the postman and he wanted me to sign for a registered letter!
这次是邮递员，他要我签收一封挂号信！
